{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJWAddvj7ZbSycY7rwZ1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QhRH7aLJTNbxjpoqaFYGKG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /work; python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('answer.md').read()\ni=s.index('**Existence'); j=s.index('**Classification')\ns=s[:i]+\"\"\"**Existence, K=2m.** Any two elements of V agree in a coordinate (e.g. (m,m,0),(m,0,m) share x_1=m), so V is internally stable by Lemma 1. (0,m,m) dominates y iff y_2<m and y_3<m; similarly for the others. So y is undominated by V iff no two coordinates are both <m, i.e. at least two coordinates are ≥m; as the sum is 2m these two equal m and the third is 0, so y∈V. Hence V is stable.\n\n\"\"\"+s[j:]\ni=s.index('(ii) If'); j=s.index('Hence every stable')\ns=s[:i]+\"\"\"(ii) If δ>0 then b<β (β−b=δ). Any t with b<t<β gives y∉V with y_2>b, y_3=K−a−t>e... (so y_2<b fails, y_3<e fails since t<β), y_1<γ alone is insufficient, so w doesn't dominate y; hence no such t exists: β=b+1, so δ=1, a+b+e=K−1, and V={(a,b,e+1),(a,b+1,e),(a+1,b,e)}. Since K≥2, (a,b,e)≠(0,0,0). If e≥1 let y=(a+1,b+1,e−1); if b≥1, y=(a+1,b−1,e+1); if a≥1, y=(a−1,b+1,e+1). In each case y is ≥ each of u,v,w in at least two coordinates (direct check), so no element of V dominates y, and y∉V: contradiction. So (ii) is impossible.\n\n\"\"\"+s[j:]\nopen('answer.md','w').write(s)\nE\ntouch SUBMIT"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2843,"cache_read_input_tokens":31418,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2843,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5325cffa-b096-4459-af67-2b0365b902a1","uuid":"88ea53e3-c188-4dc2-b876-ff838d526a55","ti